# Files never uploaded to Vercel by the CLI (`vercel`, `vercel --prod`).
#
# Why this file exists, given Vercel already has a default ignore list:
#
#   1. Vercel's defaults DO cover `.env.local` and `.env.*.local`, but they do
#      NOT cover a plain `.env`. If a `frontend/.env` is ever created it would
#      be uploaded and then LOADED BY `vite build`, baking its values into the
#      public bundle.
#   2. `.gitignore` rules are NOT applied to CLI deploys. `.gitignore` is itself
#      on Vercel's default-ignore list, so the file is not uploaded and its
#      rules never take effect. Being gitignored protects the Git-integration
#      path only.
#   3. Vite inlines every `import.meta.env.VITE_*` reference at build time, so
#      an env file that reaches the build is baked into the shipped JS and
#      cannot be undone at runtime. VITE_LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS=true in particular
#      compiles the router's sign-in guard away entirely.
#
# Ref: https://vercel.com/docs/builds/build-features#ignored-files-and-folders
# Ref: https://vercel.com/docs/deployments/vercel-ignore
#
# NOTE: this protects the UPLOAD only. It does NOT protect `vercel build` /
# `vercel deploy --prebuilt`, which build locally in this directory where
# .env.local is present on disk. Never use --prebuilt from this machine.

# Local env files (secrets + local-only feature flags)
.env
.env.*
.env.local
*.local

# Dependencies and build output — both regenerated on Vercel
node_modules
dist
